      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty strong take. Do historians generally agree that the UN is just a broken system because of the Security Council, or are there people who argue that its failures are more about the actual state of global politics than the organization itself? I've seen some people say that without the UN, things would actually be much more chaotic.",
